## Run

```sh
python3 manage.py migrate                                   # create data/app.sqlite3 (gitignored)
python3 manage.py create-account --email you@example.org --role @@ADMIN_ROLE@@   # asks for a password
python3 manage.py seed                                      # optional: load SYNTHETIC sample records
python3 manage.py serve                                     # http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

There is no default account and no default password: the first administrator is created
with `create-account` (`--password-stdin` reads the password from standard input; at least
12 characters). Options: `serve --port 0` picks a free port, `--db PATH` uses another
database file, `--secure-cookies` marks the session cookie Secure behind HTTPS.
The server binds to loopback only; see [Security](#security) before exposing it.

## Test

```sh
python3 -I manage.py test --report /tmp/report.json   # unit, API integration and acceptance tests
node tests/e2e/ui.e2e.mjs                             # browser E2E (Playwright + Chromium)
```

- Unit tests (`tests/test_validation.py`, `tests/test_migrations.py`) cover validation of
  types, required fields, maximum lengths, enumerations, defaults, PATCH merging and the migrations.
- API integration tests (`tests/test_api.py`) start the real HTTP server on a free port and
  cover CRUD for every entity, relation and uniqueness checks, sessions, roles on every
  endpoint, CSRF, security headers, pagination, sorting, filters and SQL-injection inertness.
- Acceptance tests (`tests/test_acceptance.py`) execute the @@ACCEPTANCE_COUNT@@ machine-checkable
  criteria of the specification (`app/acceptance.json`), each against a fresh server.
- The E2E test signs in, creates, edits and deletes records through the UI in every locale,
  checks labels, keyboard reachability, the focus indicator, CSP and that no request leaves
  the application origin. Set `APP_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE` to use a specific Chromium binary.
  `package.json` pins the reviewed Playwright version for `npm ci --ignore-scripts`.

